IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sga-time`
IMPORT `sga-part2`

-- sga-choice-of-fund.l4: Part 3A (sections 32A to 32ZAB) of the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992 (Commonwealth),
-- Federal Register compilation C2026C00272, plain-text conversion (not the authorised text).
-- Sections 32A (purpose) and 32B (structure) are not rules and are not encoded; NOTES.md says so.
-- The regulations, the Migration Act 1958 and the other Acts the Part points at are not among the sources: each fact the Part takes from them is a plain input.
-- Where the Part says "is made in compliance ... if" without a closing word, no limb applying is taken as non-compliance (section 32A says the Part sets out the circumstances); NOTES.md records this as a fork.

§ `Section 32C: contributions that satisfy the choice of fund requirements`

-- 32C(1): a chosen fund, or an unfunded public sector scheme (unless the employee is a Commonwealth employee who is a member of the CSS or the PSS).
-- src:736 | (1) A contribution to a fund by an employer for the benefit of an employee is made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements if the contribution is made to a fund that, at the time that the contribution is made, is:
-- src:737 | (a) a chosen fund for the employee (see Division 4); or
-- src:738 | (b) if the employee is not a Commonwealth employee who is a member of the CSS or the PSS—an unfunded public sector scheme.
-- src:739 | Contributions to stapled funds
@ref s 32C(1) (src:736-739)
GIVEN `the fund is a chosen fund for the employee at the time the contribution is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fund is an unfunded public sector scheme at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee is a Commonwealth employee who is a member of the CSS or the PSS` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`limb 32C(1) is met` MEANS
    `the fund is a chosen fund for the employee at the time the contribution is made`
    OR (`the fund is an unfunded public sector scheme at that time` AND (NOT (`the employee is a Commonwealth employee who is a member of the CSS or the PSS`)))

-- 32C(1A) and (1B): no chosen fund, and the most recent notification from the Commissioner says the fund is the stapled fund; not if a required standard choice form has not been given in time.
-- src:740 | (1A) A contribution to a fund by an employer for the benefit of an employee is made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements if, at the time the contribution is made:
-- src:741 | (a) there is no chosen fund for the employee; and
-- src:742 | (b) the most recent notification to the employer:
-- src:743 | (i) by the Commissioner; and
-- src:744 | (ii) relating to a request by the employer (or by the employer’s agent) for the Commissioner to identify any stapled fund for the employee;
-- src:745 | is that the Commissioner is satisfied that the fund is the stapled fund for the employee.
@ref s 32C(1A), (1B) (src:740-745)
-- src:746 | (1B) Subsection (1A) does not apply if, at the time the contribution is made:
-- src:747 | (a) the employer is required under section 32N to give the employee a standard choice form; and
-- src:748 | (b) the employer has not done this by the time specified in the subsection concerned.
-- src:749 | However, this subsection ceases to apply from the time that the employer gives the standard choice form to the employee.
-- src:750 | Contributions to certain eligible choice funds
@ref s 32C(1A), (1B) (src:746-750)
GIVEN `there is no chosen fund for the employee at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the most recent notification from the Commissioner, about a request to identify any stapled fund for the employee, is that the Commissioner is satisfied that the fund is the stapled fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is required under section 32N to give a standard choice form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has not given it by the time specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`limb 32C(1A) is met` MEANS
        `there is no chosen fund for the employee at the time`
    AND `the most recent notification from the Commissioner, about a request to identify any stapled fund for the employee, is that the Commissioner is satisfied that the fund is the stapled fund`
    AND (NOT (`the employer is required under section 32N to give a standard choice form` AND `the employer has not given it by the time specified`))

-- 32C(2), (2A), (2AA): no chosen fund, the Commissioner is satisfied there is no stapled fund, an eligible choice fund specified in the standard choice form (or to be), a MySuper product, and the death-benefit requirements.
-- src:751 | (2) A contribution to a fund by an employer for the benefit of an employee is made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements if, at the time the contribution is made:
-- src:752 | (a) there is no chosen fund for the employee; and
-- src:753 | (aa) the most recent notification to the employer:
-- src:754 | (i) by the Commissioner; and
-- src:755 | (ii) relating to a request by the employer (or by the employer’s agent) for the Commissioner to identify any stapled fund for the employee;
-- src:756 | is that the Commissioner is satisfied that there is no stapled fund for the employee; and
-- src:757 | (b) the fund is an eligible choice fund for the employer; and
-- src:758 | (ba) the fund:
-- src:759 | (i) is specified under section 32P in the standard choice form provided as the fund to which the employer will contribute for the benefit of the employee if the employee does not make a choice or will be so specified within the time specified in section 32N for the provision of a standard choice form to the employee; or
-- src:760 | (ii) if the employer has not contributed, and cannot contribute, to a fund (the first employer fund) that was so specified or that was purportedly so specified—will be so specified within 28 days of the employer becoming aware that the employer cannot contribute to the first employer fund; and
-- src:761 | (c) a class of beneficial interest in the fund is a MySuper product within the meaning of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993; and
-- src:762 | (d) the fund complies with the requirements (if any) set out in the regulations in relation to the provision of a benefit in respect of MySuper members of the fund that is payable only in the event of the death of the member; and
-- src:763 | (e) the fund complies with the requirements (if any) set out in the regulations in relation to offering a benefit in respect of members of the fund (other than MySuper members) that is payable only in the event of the death of the member.
@ref s 32C(2), (2A), (2AA) (src:751-763)
-- src:764 | (2A) Subsection (2) does not apply if, at the time the contribution is made:
-- src:765 | (a) the employer is required under section 32N to give the employee a standard choice form; and
-- src:766 | (b) the employer has not done this by the time specified in the subsection concerned.
-- src:767 | However, this subsection ceases to apply from the time that the employer gives the standard choice form to the employee.
@ref s 32C(2), (2A), (2AA) (src:764-767)
-- src:768 | (2AA) Paragraph (2)(ba) does not apply if the employee is, within the meaning of the Migration Act 1958, the holder of a temporary visa.
-- src:769 | Contributions to certain successor funds
@ref s 32C(2), (2A), (2AA) (src:768-769)
GIVEN `there is no chosen fund for the employee at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the most recent notification from the Commissioner is that the Commissioner is satisfied that there is no stapled fund for the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fund is an eligible choice fund for the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fund is, or will within the time allowed be, specified under section 32P in the standard choice form as the fund the employer will contribute to` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee is the holder of a temporary visa within the meaning of the Migration Act 1958` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a class of beneficial interest in the fund is a MySuper product` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fund complies with the regulations about death benefits for MySuper members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fund complies with the regulations about offering death benefits for other members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is required under section 32N to give a standard choice form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has not given it by the time specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`limb 32C(2) is met` MEANS
        `there is no chosen fund for the employee at the time`
    AND `the most recent notification from the Commissioner is that the Commissioner is satisfied that there is no stapled fund for the employee`
    AND `the fund is an eligible choice fund for the employer`
    AND (`the fund is, or will within the time allowed be, specified under section 32P in the standard choice form as the fund the employer will contribute to` OR `the employee is the holder of a temporary visa within the meaning of the Migration Act 1958`)
    AND `a class of beneficial interest in the fund is a MySuper product`
    AND `the fund complies with the regulations about death benefits for MySuper members`
    AND `the fund complies with the regulations about offering death benefits for other members`
    AND (NOT (`the employer is required under section 32N to give a standard choice form` AND `the employer has not given it by the time specified`))

-- src:770 | (2AB) A contribution to a fund (the new fund) by an employer for the benefit of an employee is made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements if:
-- src:771 | (a) the employee’s interest in the new fund was transferred to the new fund from another fund (the original fund) without the employee’s consent; and
-- src:772 | (b) at the time of the most recent contribution before the transfer to the original fund by the employer for the benefit of the employee, the original fund was a fund:
-- src:773 | (i) to which subparagraph (2)(ba)(i) applies; or
-- src:774 | (ii) to which subparagraph (2)(ba)(ii) applies, or would have applied if the transfer had not occurred; or
-- src:775 | (iii) to which subsection (1A) applies; and
-- src:776 | (c) the new fund is a successor fund (within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997) in relation to the transfer.
-- src:777 | Contributions to the CSS
@ref s 32C(2AB) (src:770-777)
GIVEN `the interest of the employee in the new fund was transferred from the original fund without the consent of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the most recent earlier contribution to the original fund it was a fund to which 32C(2)(ba)(i), 32C(2)(ba)(ii) or 32C(1A) applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new fund is a successor fund within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 in relation to the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`limb 32C(2AB) is met` MEANS
    `the interest of the employee in the new fund was transferred from the original fund without the consent of the employee`
    AND `at the time of the most recent earlier contribution to the original fund it was a fund to which 32C(2)(ba)(i), 32C(2)(ba)(ii) or 32C(1A) applied`
    AND `the new fund is a successor fund within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 in relation to the transfer`

-- 32C(3), (4), (5): the CSS, the PSS and the Superannuation (Productivity Benefit) Act 1988, unless the regulations have prescribed the law for that time.
-- src:778 | (3) A contribution to a fund by an employer for the benefit of an employee at a particular time is also made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements if the contribution is made to the CSS. However, this subsection does not apply if the law of the Commonwealth under which the contribution is made has been prescribed in relation to that time under regulations made for the purpose of this subsection.
-- src:779 | Contributions to the PSS
@ref s 32C(3), (4), (5) (src:778-779)
-- src:780 | (4) A contribution to a fund by an employer for the benefit of an employee at a particular time is also made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements if the contribution is made to the PSS. However, this subsection does not apply if the law of the Commonwealth under which the contribution is made has been prescribed in relation to that time under regulations made for the purpose of this subsection.
-- src:781 | Contributions under the Superannuation (Productivity Benefit) Act 1988
@ref s 32C(3), (4), (5) (src:780-781)
-- src:782 | (5) A contribution to a fund by an employer for the benefit of an employee at a particular time is also made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements if the contribution is made under the Superannuation (Productivity Benefit) Act 1988. However, this subsection does not apply if that Act has been prescribed in relation to that time under regulations made for the purpose of this subsection.
-- src:783 | Contributions under certain agreements and workplace determinations
@ref s 32C(3), (4), (5) (src:782-783)
GIVEN `the contribution is made to the CSS, to the PSS or under the Superannuation (Productivity Benefit) Act 1988` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations have prescribed the law for that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`limbs 32C(3) to (5) are met` MEANS
    `the contribution is made to the CSS, to the PSS or under the Superannuation (Productivity Benefit) Act 1988` AND (NOT (`the regulations have prescribed the law for that time`))

-- 32C(6) and (6AAA): industrial instruments; the workplace determination and enterprise agreement limbs need the Commissioner's stapled-fund notification and a day before 1 January 2021.
-- src:784 | (6) A contribution to a fund by an employer for the benefit of an employee is also made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements if the contribution, or a part of the contribution, is made under, or in accordance with:
-- src:785 | (a) a pre-reform certified agreement; or
-- src:786 | (b) an AWA; or
-- src:787 | (c) a pre-reform AWA; or
-- src:788 | (d) a collective agreement; or
-- src:789 | (e) an old IR agreement; or
-- src:790 | (f) an ITEA; or
-- src:791 | (g) if subsection (6AAA) applies—a workplace determination made before 1 January 2021; or
-- src:792 | (h) if subsection (6AAA) applies—an enterprise agreement made before 1 January 2021; or
-- src:793 | (i) an award mentioned in paragraph 2(2)(a) of Schedule 3 to the Fair Work (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009; or
-- src:794 | (j) a State reference transitional award or common rule.
-- src:795 | Note: A number of the expressions used in this subsection are defined in section 12A by reference to the Fair Work (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009 or the Fair Work Act 2009.
@ref s 32C(6), (6AAA) (src:784-795)
-- src:796 | (6AAA) For the purposes of paragraph (6)(g) or (h), this subsection applies if, at the time the contribution (or part of the contribution) is made, the most recent notification to the employer:
-- src:797 | (a) by the Commissioner; and
-- src:798 | (b) relating to a request by the employer (or by the employer’s agent) for the Commissioner to identify any stapled fund for the employee;
-- src:799 | is that the Commissioner is satisfied that there is no stapled fund for the employee.
-- src:800 | Contributions previously covered by paragraphs (6)(g) and (h)
@ref s 32C(6), (6AAA) (src:796-800)
GIVEN `the contribution is made under a pre-reform certified agreement, an AWA, a pre-reform AWA, a collective agreement, an old IR agreement, an ITEA, an award mentioned in paragraph 2(2)(a) of Schedule 3 to the Fair Work (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009, or a State reference transitional award or common rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contribution is made under a workplace determination or enterprise agreement made before 1 January 2021` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the most recent notification from the Commissioner is that the Commissioner is satisfied that there is no stapled fund for the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`limb 32C(6) is met` MEANS
    `the contribution is made under a pre-reform certified agreement, an AWA, a pre-reform AWA, a collective agreement, an old IR agreement, an ITEA, an award mentioned in paragraph 2(2)(a) of Schedule 3 to the Fair Work (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009, or a State reference transitional award or common rule`
    OR (`the contribution is made under a workplace determination or enterprise agreement made before 1 January 2021` AND `the most recent notification from the Commissioner is that the Commissioner is satisfied that there is no stapled fund for the employee`)

-- src:801 | (6AA) A contribution to a fund by an employer for the benefit of an employee is also made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements if:
-- src:802 | (a) at the time the contribution is made, there is no chosen fund for the employee; and
-- src:803 | (b) the fund is a fund to which the employer has previously made contributions, in compliance with the choice of fund requirements under paragraph (6)(g) or (h), for the benefit of the employee.
-- src:804 | Contributions under notional agreements preserving State awards
@ref s 32C(6AA) (src:801-804)
GIVEN `there is no chosen fund for the employee at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has previously made contributions to the fund for the employee in compliance under paragraph (6)(g) or (h)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`limb 32C(6AA) is met` MEANS
    `there is no chosen fund for the employee at the time` AND `the employer has previously made contributions to the fund for the employee in compliance under paragraph (6)(g) or (h)`

-- src:805 | (6A) A contribution to a fund by an employer for the benefit of an employee is also made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements if the contribution, or a part of the contribution, is made:
-- src:806 | (a) under, or in accordance with, a notional agreement preserving State awards; and
-- src:807 | (b) in respect of salary or wages paid before 1 July 2006.
-- src:808 | Note: A number of the expressions used in this subsection are defined in section 12A by reference to the Fair Work (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009 or the Fair Work Act 2009.
-- src:809 | Contributions under preserved State agreements
@ref s 32C(6A) (src:805-809)
GIVEN `the contribution is made under a notional agreement preserving State awards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in respect of salary or wages paid on a day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`limb 32C(6A) is met` MEANS
    `the contribution is made under a notional agreement preserving State awards` AND `a day is before 1 July 2006` `it is in respect of salary or wages paid on a day`

-- src:810 | (6B) A contribution to a fund by an employer for the benefit of an employee is also made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements if the contribution, or a part of the contribution, is made under, or in accordance with, a preserved State agreement.
-- src:811 | Note: A number of the expressions used in this subsection are defined in section 12A by reference to the Fair Work (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009 or the Fair Work Act 2009.
-- src:812 | Contributions under Division 2B State instruments
@ref s 32C(6B), (7), (8), (9) (src:810-812)
-- src:813 | (7) A contribution to a fund by an employer for the benefit of an employee is also made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements if the contribution, or a part of the contribution, is made under, or in accordance with, a Division 2B State instrument.
-- src:814 | Note: The expression Division 2B State instrument is defined in section 12A by reference to the Fair Work (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009.
-- src:815 | Contributions under State awards
@ref s 32C(6B), (7), (8), (9) (src:813-815)
-- src:816 | (8) A contribution to a fund by an employer for the benefit of an employee is also made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements if the contribution, or a part of the contribution, is made under, or in accordance with, a State industrial award.
-- src:817 | Contributions under prescribed legislation
@ref s 32C(6B), (7), (8), (9) (src:816-817)
-- src:818 | (9) A contribution to a fund by an employer for the benefit of an employee at a particular time is also made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements if the contribution is made under a law of the Commonwealth, of a State or of a Territory and the law is prescribed in relation to that time under regulations made for the purpose of this subsection.
-- src:819 | Contributions made after employees cease employment
@ref s 32C(6B), (7), (8), (9) (src:818-819)
GIVEN `the contribution is made under a preserved State agreement, a Division 2B State instrument or a State industrial award` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contribution is made under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory that the regulations prescribe for that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`limbs 32C(6B) to (9) are met` MEANS
    `the contribution is made under a preserved State agreement, a Division 2B State instrument or a State industrial award` OR `the contribution is made under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory that the regulations prescribe for that time`

-- 32CA overrides section 32C; 32C(10) treats a contribution made after employment ceases as made immediately before it ceases.
-- src:824 | 32CA Certain contributions taken not to satisfy the choice of fund requirements
-- src:825 | Despite section 32C, a contribution to a fund by an employer for the benefit of an employee is taken not to comply with the choice of fund requirements if the employer imposes a direct cost or charge on the employee as a consequence of having to contribute to that fund.
@ref s 32CA (src:824-825)
GIVEN `any limb of section 32C is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer imposes a direct cost or charge on the employee as a consequence of having to contribute to that fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the contribution is made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements` MEANS
    IF `the employer imposes a direct cost or charge on the employee as a consequence of having to contribute to that fund`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST `any limb of section 32C is met`

-- src:820 | (10) If:
-- src:821 | (a) an employee ceases to be employed by an employer; and
-- src:822 | (b) after the employment ceases, the employer makes a contribution to a fund for the benefit of the employee and in respect of the employment;
-- src:823 | then, for the purposes of this section, the contribution is taken to have been made immediately before the employment ceases.
@ref s 32C(10) (src:820-823)
GIVEN `the employment has ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contribution is made after the employment ceases, for the benefit of the employee and in respect of the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the contribution is taken to have been made immediately before the employment ceases` MEANS
    IF `the employment has ceased` AND `the contribution is made after the employment ceases, for the benefit of the employee and in respect of the employment` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 32D and 32E: eligible choice funds and funds`

-- src:827 | 32D What funds are eligible choice funds?
-- src:828 | A fund is an eligible choice fund for an employer at a particular time if:
-- src:829 | (a) it is a complying superannuation fund at that time; or
-- src:830 | (b) it is a complying superannuation scheme at that time; or
-- src:831 | (c) it is an RSA; or
-- src:832 | (ca) if the time is a time before 1 July 2006—it is the account that is continued in existence under section 8 of the Small Superannuation Accounts Act 1995 as the Superannuation Holding Accounts Special Account; or
-- src:833 | (d) at that time, paragraphs 18A(3)(a) and (d) of this Act (about defined benefit superannuation schemes) are satisfied for the fund and the employer; or
-- src:834 | (e) contributions made by the employer to the fund at that time are conclusively presumed under subsection 18A(2) of this Act to be contributions to a complying superannuation fund.
@ref s 32D (src:827-834)
GIVEN `it is a complying superannuation fund at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a complying superannuation scheme at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an RSA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time is before 1 July 2006 and it is the Superannuation Holding Accounts Special Account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraphs 18A(3)(a) and (d) are satisfied for the fund and the employer at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `contributions made by the employer to the fund at that time are conclusively presumed under subsection 18A(2) to be contributions to a complying superannuation fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is an eligible choice fund for an employer at a particular time` MEANS
    JUST (    `it is a complying superannuation fund at that time` OR `it is a complying superannuation scheme at that time` OR `it is an RSA`
           OR `the time is before 1 July 2006 and it is the Superannuation Holding Accounts Special Account`
           OR `paragraphs 18A(3)(a) and (d) are satisfied for the fund and the employer at that time`
           OR `contributions made by the employer to the fund at that time are conclusively presumed under subsection 18A(2) to be contributions to a complying superannuation fund`)

-- src:836 | (1) In this Part:
-- src:837 | fund means:
-- src:838 | (a) a superannuation fund; and
-- src:839 | (b) a superannuation scheme; and
-- src:840 | (c) an RSA;
-- src:841 | and, until immediately before 1 July 2006, includes the account that is continued in existence under section 8 of the Small Superannuation Accounts Act 1995 as the Superannuation Holding Accounts Special Account.
@ref s 32E (src:836-841)
-- src:842 | (2) For the purposes of this Part, the holder of an RSA is taken to be a member.
@ref s 32E (src:842-842)
GIVEN `is a superannuation fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a superannuation scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is an RSA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is the Superannuation Holding Accounts Special Account` IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a fund for the purposes of Part 3A` MEANS
    `is a superannuation fund` OR `is a superannuation scheme` OR `is an RSA` OR (`is the Superannuation Holding Accounts Special Account` AND `a day is before 1 July 2006` day)

§ `Division 4: choosing a fund (sections 32F to 32J)`

-- src:845 | (1) If an employee wants a fund to be a chosen fund for the employee, the employee must:
-- src:846 | (a) give the employer written notice to that effect; or
-- src:847 | (b) give the Commissioner a notice to that effect in the approved form.
-- src:848 | Note: A fund can only be a chosen fund if the employer is able to make contributions to the fund for the benefit of the employee (see subsection 32G(2)).
@ref s 32F(1) (src:845-848)
GIVEN `the employee gives the employer written notice that the employee wants the fund to be a chosen fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee gives the Commissioner a notice to that effect in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the employee has made a choice of fund` MEANS
    `the employee gives the employer written notice that the employee wants the fund to be a chosen fund` OR `the employee gives the Commissioner a notice to that effect in the approved form`

-- src:849 | (1A) If:
-- src:850 | (a) an employer has offered an employee a choice of fund before 1 July 2005; and
-- src:851 | (b) the employee has chosen a fund in accordance with the choice of funds that is offered; and
-- src:852 | (c) the limitations on that choice are consistent with section 32G or, if the choice was made before the commencement of that section, would have been consistent with section 32G if the section had been in force at the time the choice was made;
-- src:853 | then, for the purposes of this Part, any fund chosen by the employee is taken to be the chosen fund for the employee with effect from:
-- src:854 | (d) 1 July 2005; or
-- src:855 | (e) a date that is 2 months after the fund is so chosen (unless the employer determines an earlier time after 1 July 2005 but within that 2 months);
-- src:856 | whichever last occurs.
@ref s 32F(1A) (src:849-856)
GIVEN `the employer offered the employee a choice of fund on a day` IS A DATE
      `the employee chose a fund in accordance with the choice offered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the limitations on that choice are consistent with section 32G, or would have been had the section been in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the fund chosen under an offer made before 1 July 2005 is taken to be the chosen fund` MEANS
    `a day is before 1 July 2005` `the employer offered the employee a choice of fund on a day`
    AND `the employee chose a fund in accordance with the choice offered`
    AND `the limitations on that choice are consistent with section 32G, or would have been had the section been in force`

-- src:858 | (3) A fund (the selected fund) cannot become a chosen fund for an employee under this section if:
-- src:859 | (a) immediately before the employee gave the notice to the employer or the Commissioner, the employee was a defined benefit member of a defined benefit superannuation scheme; and
-- src:860 | (b) even if the selected fund were to become a chosen fund for the employee, the employee would be entitled, on the employee’s retirement, resignation or retrenchment, to the same amount of benefit from the defined benefit superannuation scheme as the employee would be entitled if the selected fund were not a chosen fund for the employee.
@ref s 32F(3) (src:858-860)
GIVEN `immediately before the notice the employee was a defined benefit member of a defined benefit superannuation scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee would be entitled on retirement, resignation or retrenchment to the same amount of benefit whether or not the selected fund were a chosen fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the selected fund cannot become a chosen fund under section 32F` MEANS
    IF `immediately before the notice the employee was a defined benefit member of a defined benefit superannuation scheme` AND `the employee would be entitled on retirement, resignation or retrenchment to the same amount of benefit whether or not the selected fund were a chosen fund`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 32FA: the employer may refuse to accept a chosen fund (1) if the employee does not provide, with the notice, the statement and the evidence; (2) if the employee has chosen another fund within the previous 12 months.
-- src:862 | (1) An employer may refuse to accept the fund chosen by an employee under section 32F and notified under paragraph 32F(1)(a) if the employee does not provide, together with the notice:
-- src:863 | (a) a written statement setting out:
-- src:864 | (i) contact details for the fund; and
-- src:865 | (ii) any other prescribed information; and
-- src:866 | (b) written evidence that the fund will accept contributions made by the employer for the benefit of the employee.
@ref s 32FA(1) (src:862-866)
GIVEN `the employee provides, together with the notice, a written statement of the contact details for the fund and any other prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee provides, together with the notice, written evidence that the fund will accept contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer may refuse to accept the fund chosen because the notice lacks the statement or the evidence` MEANS
    IF `the employee provides, together with the notice, a written statement of the contact details for the fund and any other prescribed information` AND `the employee provides, together with the notice, written evidence that the fund will accept contributions`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:867 | (2) An employer may refuse to accept the fund chosen by an employee under section 32F if the employee has chosen another fund within the previous 12 months.
@ref s 32FA(2) (src:867-867)
GIVEN `the day the employee chose another fund` IS A DATE
      `the day of the choice now notified` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer may refuse to accept the fund chosen because the employee chose another fund within the previous 12 months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `a day is on or after the day n months from` `the day the employee chose another fund` `the day of the choice now notified` (0 MINUS 12)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `within` THEN
        IF `the day the employee chose another fund` LESS THAN `the day of the choice now notified` THEN JUST `within` ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:869 | (1) The fund chosen by the employee must be an eligible choice fund for the employer at the time that the choice is made.
@ref s 32G (src:869-869)
-- src:870 | (2) The fund chosen by the employee must be a fund to which the employer can make contributions for the benefit of the employee at the time that the choice is made.
@ref s 32G (src:870-870)
GIVEN `the fund is an eligible choice fund for the employer at the time the choice is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer can make contributions to the fund for the benefit of the employee at the time the choice is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the fund chosen meets the limits on funds that may be chosen` MEANS
    `the fund is an eligible choice fund for the employer at the time the choice is made` AND `the employer can make contributions to the fund for the benefit of the employee at the time the choice is made`

-- src:872 | (1) A fund (the old fund) ceases to be a chosen fund for an employee if:
-- src:873 | (a) there is another fund that is a chosen fund for the employee; and
-- src:874 | (b) neither the employee nor the Commissioner has given the employer a written notice stating that the old fund continues to be a chosen fund for the employee.
@ref s 32H (src:872-874)
-- src:876 | (2) A fund also ceases to be a chosen fund if the employee requests the employer, under subsection 32N(3), to give him or her a standard choice form and the employer does not do this by the time specified in that subsection.
@ref s 32H (src:876-876)
-- src:877 | (3) A fund also ceases to be a chosen fund if it is impossible for the employer to contribute on behalf of the employee to the chosen fund. This may occur immediately after the fund becomes a chosen fund for the employee.
-- src:878 | Example: The chosen fund is closed to new members or ceases to accept further contributions.
@ref s 32H (src:877-878)
-- src:879 | (4) A fund also ceases to be a chosen fund if the fund ceases to be an eligible choice fund for the employer. This may occur immediately after the fund becomes a chosen fund for the employee.
@ref s 32H (src:879-879)
GIVEN `there is another fund that is a chosen fund for the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `neither the employee nor the Commissioner has given the employer written notice that the old fund continues to be a chosen fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee requested a standard choice form under subsection 32N(3) and the employer did not give it by the time specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is impossible for the employer to contribute on behalf of the employee to the chosen fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fund has ceased to be an eligible choice fund for the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a fund ceases to be a chosen fund` MEANS
    JUST (    (`there is another fund that is a chosen fund for the employee` AND `neither the employee nor the Commissioner has given the employer written notice that the old fund continues to be a chosen fund`)
           OR `the employee requested a standard choice form under subsection 32N(3) and the employer did not give it by the time specified`
           OR `it is impossible for the employer to contribute on behalf of the employee to the chosen fund`
           OR `the fund has ceased to be an eligible choice fund for the employer`)

-- src:875 | (1A) The employee may give the employer a written notice, or give the Commissioner a notice in the approved form, stating that the old fund continues to be a chosen fund for the employee.
@ref s 32H(1A) (src:875-875)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employee may give notice that the old fund continues to be a chosen fund` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- src:880 | 32J A successor fund may become a chosen fund
-- src:881 | For the purposes of this Act, if:
-- src:882 | (a) an employee’s interest in a superannuation fund (the original fund) is transferred to another superannuation fund without the consent of the member; and
-- src:883 | (b) the other fund is a successor fund (within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997) in relation to the transfer; and
-- src:884 | (c) immediately before the transfer takes effect, the original fund was a chosen fund for the employee; and
-- src:885 | (d) at the time the transfer takes effect, the other fund:
-- src:886 | (i) is an eligible choice fund; and
-- src:887 | (ii) is a fund to which the employer can make contributions for the benefit of the employee;
-- src:888 | from the time the transfer takes effect, the other fund is taken to be a chosen fund for the employee, and the original fund is taken no longer to be a chosen fund for the employee.
@ref s 32J (src:880-888)
GIVEN `the interest of the employee was transferred to another superannuation fund without the consent of the member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other fund is a successor fund within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 in relation to the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `immediately before the transfer takes effect the original fund was a chosen fund for the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the transfer takes effect the other fund is an eligible choice fund and a fund to which the employer can make contributions for the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the other fund is taken to be a chosen fund from the time the transfer takes effect` MEANS
    IF `the interest of the employee was transferred to another superannuation fund without the consent of the member`
       AND `the other fund is a successor fund within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 in relation to the transfer`
       AND `immediately before the transfer takes effect the original fund was a chosen fund for the employee`
       AND `at the time the transfer takes effect the other fund is an eligible choice fund and a fund to which the employer can make contributions for the employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Division 6: standard choice forms (sections 32N to 32P)`

DECLARE `Trigger for a standard choice form` IS ONE OF
    `the employee was employed by the employer on 1 July 2005`
    `the employee first commenced employment with the employer`
    `the employee gave the employer a written request`
    `the employer became aware that there ceased to be any chosen fund because of subsection 32H(3) or (4)`
    `the employer changed the fund it contributes to under subsection 32C(2)`
    `the employer first became aware that it cannot contribute to the employer fund`

-- src:891 | (1) An employer must give a standard choice form before 29 July 2005 to each employee employed by the employer on 1 July 2005.
@ref s 32N(1) to (5A) (src:891-891)
-- src:893 | (2) An employer must give a standard choice form to an employee within 28 days of the employee first commencing employment with the employer.
-- src:894 | (3) An employer must also give a standard choice form to an employee within 28 days of the employee giving the employer a written request to do so. However, a request is taken never to have been made if the employee has been given a standard choice form within the previous 12 months.
@ref s 32N(1) to (5A) (src:893-894)
-- src:895 | (4) An employer must also give a standard choice form to an employee within 28 days of the employer becoming aware that there ceased to be any chosen fund for the employee because of:
-- src:896 | (a) subsection 32H(3) (employer unable to contribute to fund); or
-- src:897 | (b) subsection 32H(4) (fund ceasing to be eligible choice fund).
-- src:898 | (5) An employer must also give a standard choice form to an employee if:
-- src:899 | (a) the employer is making contributions, in accordance with subsection 32C(2), to a fund for the benefit of the employee; and
-- src:900 | (b) the employer changes the fund to which the employer makes contributions, in accordance with that subsection, for the benefit of the employee.
-- src:901 | The standard choice form must be given within 28 days after the change.
-- src:902 | (5A) An employer must also give a standard choice form (the updated standard choice form) to an employee if:
-- src:903 | (a) the employer has specified a fund (the employer fund) in a standard choice form as the fund to which the employer will contribute under subsection 32C(2) in the event of the employee failing to make a choice of fund; and
-- src:904 | (b) the employer discovers, after giving an employee the standard choice form, that the employer cannot contribute to the employer fund for the benefit of the employee.
-- src:905 | The updated standard choice form must be given within 28 days after the employer first becomes aware that the employer cannot contribute to the employer fund for the benefit of the employee.
@ref s 32N(1) to (5A) (src:895-905)
GIVEN trigger IS A `Trigger for a standard choice form`
      `the day of the trigger` IS A DATE
      `the day the form is given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a standard choice form is given in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER trigger
    WHEN `the employee was employed by the employer on 1 July 2005` THEN JUST (`a day is before 29 July 2005` `the day the form is given`)
    WHEN `the employee first commenced employment with the employer` THEN within
    WHEN `the employee gave the employer a written request` THEN within
    WHEN `the employer became aware that there ceased to be any chosen fund because of subsection 32H(3) or (4)` THEN within
    WHEN `the employer changed the fund it contributes to under subsection 32C(2)` THEN within
    WHEN `the employer first became aware that it cannot contribute to the employer fund` THEN within
    WHERE
        within MEANS `an act is within n days of an event` `the day the form is given` `the day of the trigger` 28

-- src:894 | (3) An employer must also give a standard choice form to an employee within 28 days of the employee giving the employer a written request to do so. However, a request is taken never to have been made if the employee has been given a standard choice form within the previous 12 months.
@ref s 32N(3), (6) (src:894-894)
-- src:906 | (6) An employer may also give a standard choice form at any time.
@ref s 32N(3), (6) (src:906-906)
GIVEN `the employee has been given a standard choice form within the previous 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a written request for a standard choice form is taken never to have been made` MEANS
    IF `the employee has been given a standard choice form within the previous 12 months` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Exceptions under section 32NA` HAS
    `the employee has chosen a fund under section 32F by the time specified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer makes contributions of a kind in 32C(3) to (9) in compliance with the choice of fund requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee chose a fund before 1 July 2005 that is taken to be the chosen fund under 32F(1A), and 32N(3) and (4) do not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee is a member of an unfunded public sector scheme and is not a Commonwealth employee who is a member of the CSS or the PSS` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee ceases to be an employee before the end of the period for giving the form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a condition of employment that the employee choose from all eligible choice funds and the employer has no arrangement to pay to a default fund` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee is a defined benefit member and subsection 20B(2) applies for the QE day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee is a defined benefit member and subsection 20B(3) applies for the QE day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee is a defined benefit member and would be entitled to the same benefit whether or not contributions are made to another fund` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee is covered by a notional agreement preserving State awards or a preserved State agreement and the employer gave the State law notification` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee is the holder of a temporary visa within the meaning of the Migration Act 1958` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:908 | (1) An employer is not required under section 32N to give an employee a standard choice form if the employee has chosen a fund under section 32F by the time specified in subsection 32N(1), (2), (3) or (4).
@ref s 32NA (src:908-908)
-- src:909 | (2) An employer is not required under section 32N to give an employee a standard choice form if:
-- src:910 | (a) the employer is making contributions of a kind mentioned in subsections 32C(3) to (9) for the benefit of the employee; and
-- src:911 | (b) the contributions are made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements.
@ref s 32NA (src:909-911)
-- src:912 | (3) Subject to subsections 32N(3) and (4), an employer is not required under section 32N to give an employee a standard choice form if:
-- src:913 | (a) the employee has chosen a fund before 1 July 2005; and
-- src:914 | (b) the fund so chosen is to be taken, in accordance with subsection 32F(1A), to be the chosen fund for that employee.
@ref s 32NA (src:912-914)
-- src:915 | (4) An employer is not required under section 32N to give an employee a standard choice form if the employee:
-- src:916 | (a) is a member of an unfunded public sector scheme; and
-- src:917 | (b) is not a Commonwealth employee who is a member of the CSS or the PSS.
@ref s 32NA (src:915-917)
-- src:918 | (5) An employer is not required under section 32N to give an employee a standard choice form if the employee ceases to be an employee before the end of the period for giving a standard choice form to the employee.
@ref s 32NA (src:918-918)
-- src:919 | (6) An employer is not required under section 32N to give an employee a standard choice form if:
-- src:920 | (a) it is a condition of the employment of that employee that the employee choose a fund from funds that include all funds that are eligible choice funds for the employer at the time the choice is made; and
-- src:921 | (b) the employer does not have an arrangement to pay contributions to a fund for the benefit of an employee in the event that the employee failed or refused to choose a fund.
@ref s 32NA (src:919-921)
-- src:922 | (7) An employer is not required under section 32N to give an employee a standard choice form for a QE day if:
-- src:923 | (a) the employee is a defined benefit member of a defined benefit superannuation scheme; and
-- src:924 | (b) subsection 20B(2) applies to the employer for the employee, the scheme and the QE day.
@ref s 32NA (src:922-924)
-- src:925 | (8) An employer is not required under section 32N to give an employee a standard choice form for a QE day if:
-- src:926 | (a) the employee is a defined benefit member of a defined benefit superannuation scheme; and
-- src:927 | (b) subsection 20B(3) applies to the employer for the employee, the scheme and the QE day in relation to the defined benefit that has accrued to the employee under the scheme.
@ref s 32NA (src:925-927)
-- src:928 | (9) An employer is not required under section 32N to give an employee a standard choice form if:
-- src:929 | (a) the employee is a defined benefit member of a defined benefit superannuation scheme; and
-- src:930 | (b) the employee would be entitled, on the employee’s retirement, resignation or retrenchment, to the same amount of benefit from the defined benefit superannuation scheme, whether or not the employee had contributions made by the employer for his or her benefit to a fund other than the defined benefit superannuation scheme.
@ref s 32NA (src:928-930)
-- src:931 | (10) An employer is not required under section 32N to give an employee a standard choice form if:
-- src:932 | (a) the employee is covered by a notional agreement preserving State awards or a preserved State agreement; and
-- src:933 | (b) before the commencement of Schedule 1 to the Workplace Relations Amendment (Work Choices) Act 2005, the employer was required, under a State law, to give the employee a notification that the employee can choose a superannuation fund; and
-- src:934 | (c) the employer has given the notification mentioned in paragraph (b) to the employee.
@ref s 32NA (src:931-934)
-- src:935 | (11) An employer is not required under section 32N to give an employee a standard choice form if the employee is, within the meaning of the Migration Act 1958, the holder of a temporary visa.
@ref s 32NA (src:935-935)
GIVEN e IS AN `Exceptions under section 32NA`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the employer is not required under section 32N to give a standard choice form` MEANS
    `first half` OR `second half`
    WHERE
        `first half` MEANS e's `the employee has chosen a fund under section 32F by the time specified` OR e's `the employer makes contributions of a kind in 32C(3) to (9) in compliance with the choice of fund requirements` OR e's `the employee chose a fund before 1 July 2005 that is taken to be the chosen fund under 32F(1A), and 32N(3) and (4) do not apply` OR e's `the employee is a member of an unfunded public sector scheme and is not a Commonwealth employee who is a member of the CSS or the PSS` OR e's `the employee ceases to be an employee before the end of the period for giving the form` OR e's `it is a condition of employment that the employee choose from all eligible choice funds and the employer has no arrangement to pay to a default fund`
        `second half` MEANS e's `the employee is a defined benefit member and subsection 20B(2) applies for the QE day` OR e's `the employee is a defined benefit member and subsection 20B(3) applies for the QE day` OR e's `the employee is a defined benefit member and would be entitled to the same benefit whether or not contributions are made to another fund` OR e's `the employee is covered by a notional agreement preserving State awards or a preserved State agreement and the employer gave the State law notification` OR e's `the employee is the holder of a temporary visa within the meaning of the Migration Act 1958`

-- 32N: the employer must give a form when a trigger has occurred and no exception under 32NA applies.
-- src:891 | (1) An employer must give a standard choice form before 29 July 2005 to each employee employed by the employer on 1 July 2005.
-- src:892 | Note: An employer does not have to provide a standard choice form to an existing employee except in the specific circumstances outlined in this section. See also the further exceptions in section 32NA.
@ref s 32N (src:891-892)
-- src:893 | (2) An employer must give a standard choice form to an employee within 28 days of the employee first commencing employment with the employer.
@ref s 32N (src:893-893)
-- src:894 | (3) An employer must also give a standard choice form to an employee within 28 days of the employee giving the employer a written request to do so. However, a request is taken never to have been made if the employee has been given a standard choice form within the previous 12 months.
@ref s 32N (src:894-894)
-- src:895 | (4) An employer must also give a standard choice form to an employee within 28 days of the employer becoming aware that there ceased to be any chosen fund for the employee because of:
-- src:896 | (a) subsection 32H(3) (employer unable to contribute to fund); or
-- src:897 | (b) subsection 32H(4) (fund ceasing to be eligible choice fund).
@ref s 32N (src:895-897)
-- src:898 | (5) An employer must also give a standard choice form to an employee if:
-- src:899 | (a) the employer is making contributions, in accordance with subsection 32C(2), to a fund for the benefit of the employee; and
-- src:900 | (b) the employer changes the fund to which the employer makes contributions, in accordance with that subsection, for the benefit of the employee.
-- src:901 | The standard choice form must be given within 28 days after the change.
@ref s 32N (src:898-901)
-- src:902 | (5A) An employer must also give a standard choice form (the updated standard choice form) to an employee if:
-- src:903 | (a) the employer has specified a fund (the employer fund) in a standard choice form as the fund to which the employer will contribute under subsection 32C(2) in the event of the employee failing to make a choice of fund; and
-- src:904 | (b) the employer discovers, after giving an employee the standard choice form, that the employer cannot contribute to the employer fund for the benefit of the employee.
-- src:905 | The updated standard choice form must be given within 28 days after the employer first becomes aware that the employer cannot contribute to the employer fund for the benefit of the employee.
@ref s 32N (src:902-905)
GIVEN `a trigger in section 32N has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is not required under section 32N to give a standard choice form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer must give a standard choice form` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the employer is not required under section 32N to give a standard choice form` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `a trigger in section 32N has occurred` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:937 | (1) For the purposes of this Part, a standard choice form is a form that is in writing and that contains the following information:
-- src:938 | (a) a statement that the employee may choose any eligible choice fund for the employer as a chosen fund for the employee;
-- src:939 | (c) the name of the fund that the employer will contribute to if the employee does not make a choice;
-- src:940 | (e) other information that is required, under the regulations, to be included in the form;
-- src:941 | (g) if the employee is a member of a defined benefits scheme—information in relation to that scheme that is required, under the regulations, to be included.
@ref s 32P (src:937-941)
-- src:942 | (2) The regulations may require additional information in relation to funds to be made available to employees and may prescribe where and when such information is to be made available.
@ref s 32P (src:942-942)
GIVEN `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the employee may choose any eligible choice fund for the employer as a chosen fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it gives the name of the fund the employer will contribute to if the employee does not make a choice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it contains other information required under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee is a member of a defined benefits scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it contains the information about that scheme required under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a standard choice form` MEANS
        `it is in writing`
    AND `it states that the employee may choose any eligible choice fund for the employer as a chosen fund`
    AND `it gives the name of the fund the employer will contribute to if the employee does not make a choice`
    AND `it contains other information required under the regulations`
    AND (IF `the employee is a member of a defined benefits scheme` THEN `it contains the information about that scheme required under the regulations` ELSE TRUE)

§ `Division 7: stapled funds (sections 32Q and 32R)`

-- src:944 | 32Q What is the stapled fund for an employee
-- src:945 | A fund is the stapled fund, for an employee at a particular time, if the requirements prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this section are met in relation to the fund at that time.
@ref s 32Q (src:944-945)
GIVEN `the requirements prescribed by the regulations are met in relation to the fund at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is the stapled fund for an employee at a particular time` MEANS
    IF `the requirements prescribed by the regulations are met in relation to the fund at that time` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:948 | (1) An employer, or the employer’s agent, may request the Commissioner to identify any stapled fund for an employee of the employer. Such a request must be:
-- src:949 | (a) in the approved form; and
-- src:950 | (b) made in accordance with any requirements prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph.
@ref s 32R(1), (1A) (src:948-950)
-- src:951 | (1A) Such a request may be made before, at or after the time the employee is given a standard choice form under Division 6.
-- src:952 | Considering and responding to requests
@ref s 32R(1), (1A) (src:951-952)
GIVEN `the request is in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is made in accordance with any requirements prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a request to identify any stapled fund meets section 32R(1)` MEANS
    `the request is in the approved form` AND `the request is made in accordance with any requirements prescribed by the regulations`

-- src:953 | (2) Upon being given such a request by an employer (or by the employer’s agent), the Commissioner must:
-- src:954 | (a) consider the request; and
-- src:955 | (b) notify in writing the employer (and the employer’s agent if the agent made the request):
-- src:956 | (i) whether the Commissioner is satisfied that there is a stapled fund for the employee; and
-- src:957 | (ii) if the Commissioner is satisfied that there is a stapled fund for the employee—about the details necessary for the employer to make contributions to that fund for the benefit of the employee;
-- src:958 | as soon as practicable and in accordance with any requirements prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this subsection.
-- src:959 | Changes to earlier notifications
@ref s 32R(2) (src:953-959)
GIVEN `the request was made by the agent of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner is satisfied that there is a stapled fund for the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`what the Commissioner must notify in writing, and to whom` MEANS
    BRANCH IF agent AND satisfied THEN LIST "to the employer and the employer's agent: that the Commissioner is satisfied that there is a stapled fund", "to the employer and the employer's agent: the details necessary for the employer to make contributions to that fund"
           IF agent THEN LIST "to the employer and the employer's agent: that the Commissioner is not satisfied that there is a stapled fund"
           IF satisfied THEN LIST "to the employer: that the Commissioner is satisfied that there is a stapled fund", "to the employer: the details necessary for the employer to make contributions to that fund"
           OTHERWISE LIST "to the employer: that the Commissioner is not satisfied that there is a stapled fund"
    WHERE
        agent MEANS `the request was made by the agent of the employer`
        satisfied MEANS `the Commissioner is satisfied that there is a stapled fund for the employee`

-- src:960 | (3) The Commissioner may, in any circumstances prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this subsection, change an earlier notification given in relation to the employee. The Commissioner must give written notice of the change as soon as practicable to:
-- src:961 | (a) the employer; and
-- src:962 | (b) if the earlier notification arose from a request by the employer’s agent—the employer’s agent.
@ref s 32R(3) (src:960-962)
GIVEN `the earlier notification arose from a request by the agent of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`who the Commissioner must give written notice of a change to an earlier notification` MEANS
    IF `the earlier notification arose from a request by the agent of the employer` THEN LIST "the employer", "the employer's agent" ELSE LIST "the employer"

§ `Division 8: miscellaneous (sections 32W to 32ZA)`

-- src:964 | 32W Disclosing tax file numbers provided in standard choice forms
-- src:965 | A taxation officer (within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997) may disclose another person’s tax file number (within the meaning of that Act) if:
-- src:966 | (a) the other person provided the number to the Commissioner in a notice given to the Commissioner under paragraph 32F(1)(b); and
-- src:967 | (b) the disclosure is to the other person’s employer.
@ref s 32W (src:964-967)
GIVEN `the other person provided the number to the Commissioner in a notice under paragraph 32F(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is to the other person's employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a taxation officer may disclose the tax file number` MEANS
    IF `the other person provided the number to the Commissioner in a notice under paragraph 32F(1)(b)` AND `the disclosure is to the other person's employer` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:968 | 32X Application of Part to different employers of an employee
-- src:969 | This Part applies separately to each employer of an employee. For example, a fund that is a chosen fund of an employee as a result of a standard choice form being given by an employer is only a chosen fund in relation to the operation of these provisions to that employer.
@ref s 32X (src:968-969)
GIVEN `the fund is a chosen fund because of a standard choice form given by the employer asked about` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the fund is a chosen fund in relation to a different employer of the employee` MEANS JUST FALSE

-- src:970 | 32Z Contributions satisfy Commonwealth or Territory industrial award requirements—chosen funds and stapled funds etc.
-- src:971 | A requirement in a Commonwealth industrial award or a Territory industrial award that an employer make contributions to a superannuation fund on behalf of an employee is not enforceable to the extent that the employer instead makes the contributions on behalf of the employee to another superannuation fund:
-- src:972 | (a) in compliance with this Part in a case where the other fund is a chosen fund for the employee; or
-- src:973 | (b) in compliance with subsection 32C(1A) (about contributions to stapled funds); or
-- src:974 | (c) in compliance with subsection 32C(2AB) in a case where subparagraph 32C(2AB)(b)(iii) applies (about contributions to a successor fund of a stapled fund).
@ref s 32Z, 32ZAA (src:970-974)
-- src:975 | 32ZAA Contributions satisfy State or Territory law requirements—chosen funds and stapled funds etc.
-- src:976 | (1) This section applies to an employer that is a corporation to which paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution applies.
-- src:977 | (2) A requirement in a law of a State or Territory that the employer make contributions to a superannuation fund on behalf of an employee is not enforceable to the extent that the employer instead makes the contributions on behalf of the employee to another superannuation fund:
-- src:978 | (a) in compliance with this Part in a case where the other fund is a chosen fund for the employee; or
-- src:979 | (b) in compliance with subsection 32C(1A) (about contributions to stapled funds); or
-- src:980 | (c) in compliance with subsection 32C(2AB) in a case where subparagraph 32C(2AB)(b)(iii) applies (about contributions to a successor fund of a stapled fund).
@ref s 32Z, 32ZAA (src:975-980)
GIVEN `the requirement is in a Commonwealth or Territory industrial award, or in a law of a State or Territory and the employer is a corporation to which paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer instead makes the contributions to another fund in compliance with this Part where that fund is a chosen fund, or in compliance with subsection 32C(1A), or in compliance with subsection 32C(2AB) where subparagraph (2AB)(b)(iii) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the requirement to contribute to a fund is enforceable to the extent the employer contributes instead` MEANS
    IF `the requirement is in a Commonwealth or Territory industrial award, or in a law of a State or Territory and the employer is a corporation to which paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution applies` AND `the employer instead makes the contributions to another fund in compliance with this Part where that fund is a chosen fund, or in compliance with subsection 32C(1A), or in compliance with subsection 32C(2AB) where subparagraph (2AB)(b)(iii) applies`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:981 | 32ZAB Effect of blocking contributions to PSSAP etc.—eligible choice funds
-- src:982 | (1) This section applies if:
-- src:983 | (a) an employer cannot make contributions to a superannuation fund on behalf of an employee because of section 60F of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 (consequences of 2 consecutive fail assessments); and
-- src:984 | (b) the superannuation fund is any of the following:
-- src:985 | (i) PSSAP;
-- src:986 | (ii) ADF Super (within the meaning of the Australian Defence Force Superannuation Act 2015);
-- src:987 | (iii) if the regulations made for the purposes of this subparagraph specify another superannuation fund—that superannuation fund.
-- src:988 | (2) The following provisions do not have effect in relation to the superannuation fund:
-- src:989 | (a) if the superannuation fund is PSSAP—section 16 of the Superannuation Act 2005;
-- src:990 | (b) if the superannuation fund is ADF Super (within the meaning of the Australian Defence Force Superannuation Act 2015)—section 15 of that Act;
-- src:991 | (c) if the superannuation fund is another superannuation fund—a provision that:
-- src:992 | (i) is specified in regulations made for the purposes of this subparagraph; and
-- src:993 | (ii) is analogous to the provisions mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b).
@ref s 32ZAB (src:981-993)
GIVEN `the employer cannot make contributions because of section 60F of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fund is PSSAP, ADF Super or a fund the regulations specify` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the blocking provisions have effect in relation to the fund` MEANS
    IF `the employer cannot make contributions because of section 60F of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993` AND `the fund is PSSAP, ADF Super or a fund the regulations specify`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:994 | 32ZA Employers not liable for damages
-- src:995 | An employer is not liable to compensate any person for loss or damage arising from anything done by the employer in complying with this Part.
@ref s 32ZA (src:994-995)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer is liable to compensate a person for loss or damage arising from anything done in complying with Part 3A` MEANS JUST FALSE
